The failures after the rebase are fixed with a one-line change, and all five lanes now pass. But I couldn't amend the commit: every git write was refused with "This command requires approval". The fix is an unstaged change in the working tree on top of `b86984d0`, and nothing else is modified.

**Cause.** My three `dao.space.dht` host functions (`load-index`, `load-status`, `q`) returned a plain `{:effect ::call …}` map. After D4, only effects minted by `module/make-effect` are performed, so those maps printed as data. That accounts for all of the landing failures (JVM 7, Node 5, Dart 1), in the REPL host-function test and the host-function steps of the process test.

**Fix.** In `src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc`, `dht-export` now returns `(module/make-effect ::call {:op (get dht-ops sym), :args (vec args)})`. That mirrors D4's own change to the `q` export. The call handler still reads `:op` from the effect, and the exports' profiles already declare `::call`, so D4's effect-kind check passes. No D4 code changed, and nothing in D4 blocked S5.

